From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Ellis <kevers@google.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:20:34 -0700
Subject: Do not composite backdrop-filter animations with reference filters

Regular `filter` animations reject reference filters (`url(#...)`)
from running on the compositor because `ReferenceFilterOperation::MovesPixels returns true. Because
pixel-moving `backdrop-filter` operations (such as `blur()` and
`drop-shadow()`) do not affect layer bounds,
`CompositorAnimations::CheckCanStartEffectOnCompositor` previously had
no per-keyframe filter check for `kBackdropFilter`, inadvertently
allowing reference filters onto the compositor. Reference filters must
fall back to the main thread for two reasons:
1. Reference filters are not interpolable; on the main thread they
   animate discretely at 50% progress, whereas
   `cc::FilterOperations::Blend` returns the destination filter
   across the entire active interval when either endpoint contains a
   reference filter.
2. Building compositor filter keyframes in `AddKeyframeToCurve` calls
   `FilterEffectBuilder::BuildFilterOperations` during
   `DocumentAnimations::UpdateAnimations` (post-paint) with an empty
   reference box, which can synchronously paint referenced SVG
   resource subtrees (such as `<feImage>`) outside the paint lifecycle
   phase.

Bug: 575318807
Change-Id: I54b5f2a3b93fe2a1cb0794d1bcf81eb6edfbe798
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8674102
